[Cheonji Ilbo, Yeosu = Reporter Lee Bong-hwa] With about 460 days left until the opening of the 2026 Yeosu World Island Expo, preparations are intensifying, including confirmation of participating countries, attracting visitors, and planning for post-expo utilization.

Participation from island nations such as Palau and Cebu has been confirmed, expanding international cooperation, and the target number of visitors has been set at 3 million.

Post-expo utilization plans are being developed to create sustainable tourism assets, including the &lsquo;Light Island Project.&rsquo;

Citizens voice concerns about side effects such as ecological damage and traffic inconveniences, calling for an expo centered on resident participation.

Special Commissioner Kim Cheol-min emphasizes developing content that reflects the lives of island residents and making a tangible contribution to the local economy.

The expo asks us:

&ldquo;With whom and in what way should the future of islands be created?&rdquo;
